- body: "A fixed publication plan for an owned isolated repository. Reverify renamed LexLean source in an identity-addressed publication manifest with the same Rule30UOR module and theorem namespace before using its attested generated Lean artifact. Publish the paper statement through theorem registration without adding a second copy of the host declaration to the paper entrypoints. Register generated host modules and theorem lexemes through the existing r30 API; change frontier status only for a checked closed claim. Retain each commit at its own evidence-and-commit-addressed reference, making repeated retention idempotent without replacing a different publication commit. Commit through the unchanged hook and push only against the exact predecessor with a source-branch lease. No shell command strings, remote models or receipt-based shortcuts. This plan supplies jobs; only the enclosing publication lifecycle establishes their ordering, ownership and successful completion.",
